      "heading": "Arithmetic sequences",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q": "Find the 12th term of the arithmetic sequence $5,\\,9,\\,13,\\ldots$",
          "answer": "$a_1=5$, $d=4$. $a_{12}=5+(11)(4)=49$."
        },
        {
          "q": "The 4th term of an arithmetic sequence is 18, and the 9th term is 38. Find the first term and the common difference.",
          "answer": "$a_1+3d=18$ and $a_1+8d=38$. Subtracting: $5d=20\\Rightarrow d=4$, so $a_1=18-12=6$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Find the sum of the first 20 terms of the arithmetic sequence $7,\\,11,\\,15,\\ldots$",
          "answer": "$a_1=7$, $d=4$, $a_{20}=7+(19)(4)=83$. $S_{20}=\\dfrac{20}{2}(7+83)=10(90)=900$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Find the number of terms in the arithmetic sequence $6,\\,10,\\,14,\\ldots,150$.",
          "answer": "$a_1=6$, $d=4$. $6+4(n-1)=150\\Rightarrow4(n-1)=144\\Rightarrow n-1=36\\Rightarrow n=37$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Geometric sequences",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q": "Find the 7th term of the geometric sequence $3,\\,6,\\,12,\\ldots$",
          "answer": "$a_1=3$, $r=2$. $a_7=3(2^6)=3(64)=192$."
        },
        {
          "q": "In a geometric sequence with all positive terms, the 3rd term is 20 and the 5th term is 80. Find $r$ and $a_1$.",
          "answer": "$a_1r^2=20$ and $a_1r^4=80$. Dividing: $r^2=4$, and since all terms are positive, $r=2$. Then $a_1=\\dfrac{20}{4}=5$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Given that $x-1$, $x+1$, and $3x-1$ are consecutive terms of a geometric sequence, find the possible value(s) of $x$.",
          "answer": "$(x+1)^2=(x-1)(3x-1)\\Rightarrow x^2+2x+1=3x^2-4x+1\\Rightarrow0=2x^2-6x=2x(x-3)$. So $x=0$ or $x=3$. If $x=0$, the terms are $-1,1,-1$ (ratio $-1$, valid). If $x=3$, the terms are $2,4,8$ (ratio $2$, valid)."
        },
        {
          "q": "Find the sum of the first 6 terms of the geometric sequence $5,\\,15,\\,45,\\ldots$",
          "answer": "$a_1=5$, $r=3$. $S_6=\\dfrac{5(3^6-1)}{3-1}=\\dfrac{5(728)}{2}=1820$."
        }
      ]
