        {
          "q": "Simplify $\\dfrac{4+3i}{1-2i}$ by multiplying by the conjugate of the denominator.",
          "answer": "$\\dfrac{4+3i}{1-2i}\\cdot\\dfrac{1+2i}{1+2i}=\\dfrac{(4+3i)(1+2i)}{1^2+2^2}=\\dfrac{4+8i+3i+6i^2}{5}=\\dfrac{-2+11i}{5}=-\\dfrac{2}{5}+\\dfrac{11}{5}i$."
